IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc28-part24-s752`
IMPORT `ccc28-part24c-hearing-appeal`

-- ccc28-tests-part24c.l4 -- tests of sections 757 to 761. Expected values are written by hand from the words of each provision, on both sides of every threshold.

§ `s 757: evidence of character and repute`

#ASSERT `s 757 evidence of character and repute may be admitted` TRUE `s 757(a) the question of whether the offender is or is not a dangerous offender or a long-term offender` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 757 evidence of character and repute may be admitted` TRUE `s 757(b) a sentence to be imposed or an order to be made under this Part` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 757 evidence of character and repute may be admitted` TRUE `s 757 another purpose` EQUALS NOTHING   -- list not closed
#ASSERT `s 757 evidence of character and repute may be admitted` FALSE `s 757(a) the question of whether the offender is or is not a dangerous offender or a long-term offender` EQUALS NOTHING   -- "if the court thinks fit": a grant limited by an "if"
#ASSERT `s 757 evidence of character and repute may be admitted` FALSE `s 757 another purpose` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 758: presence of the offender at the hearing`

#ASSERT `s 758(1) the offender shall be present at the hearing of the application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 758(1) the offender shall be present at the hearing of the application` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Notwithstanding subsection (1)": the court acted under subsection (2)
#ASSERT `s 758(1) the offender shall be present at the hearing of the application` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no hearing of an application under this Part
#ASSERT `s 758(1)(a) the court may order the person having the custody of the accused to bring the offender before the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 758(1)(a) the court may order the person having the custody of the accused to bring the offender before the court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not confined: a grant limited by an "if"
#ASSERT `s 758(1)(b) the court shall issue a summons or a warrant to compel the accused to attend before the court` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 758(1)(b) the court shall issue a summons or a warrant to compel the accused to attend before the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- confined in a prison: paragraph (a) applies instead
#TRACE `s 758(1)(a) the court's power to order the person having the custody to bring the offender` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 758(1)(a) order in writing the person having the custody of the accused to bring the offender before the court` AT 3

#ASSERT `s 758(2)(a) the court may cause the offender to be removed and kept out of court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 758(2)(a) the court may cause the offender to be removed and kept out of court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- misconduct, but continuing in his presence would be feasible
#ASSERT `s 758(2)(a) the court may cause the offender to be removed and kept out of court` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no misconduct by interrupting
#ASSERT `s 758(2)(b) the court may permit the offender to be out of court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 758(2)(b) the court may permit the offender to be out of court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 759: appeals`

#ASSERT `s 759(1) the offender may appeal to the court of appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 759 a ground of law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 759(1) the offender may appeal to the court of appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 759 a ground of fact` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 759(1) the offender may appeal to the court of appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 759 a ground of mixed law and fact` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 759(1) the offender may appeal to the court of appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 759 another ground` EQUALS NOTHING   -- list not closed
#ASSERT `s 759(1) the offender may appeal to the court of appeal` FALSE TRUE `s 759 a ground of law` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender: a named class
#ASSERT `s 759(1) the offender may appeal to the court of appeal` TRUE FALSE `s 759 a ground of law` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not from a decision made under this Part
#ASSERT `s 759(2) the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal` TRUE `s 759 a ground of law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 759(2) the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal` TRUE `s 759 a ground of fact` EQUALS NOTHING   -- "on any ground of law": limited by its own wording
#ASSERT `s 759(2) the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal` TRUE `s 759 a ground of mixed law and fact` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 759(2) the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal` TRUE `s 759 another ground` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 759(2) the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal` FALSE `s 759 a ground of law` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not from a decision made under this Part
#ASSERT `s 759(3) the court of appeal may make this disposition` `s 759(3)(a)(i) allow the appeal and find that an offender is or is not a dangerous offender or a long-term offender or impose a sentence or make an order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 759(3) the court of appeal may make this disposition` `s 759(3)(a)(ii) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, with any directions that the court considers appropriate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 759(3) the court of appeal may make this disposition` `s 759(3)(b) dismiss the appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 759(3) the court of appeal may make this disposition` `s 759(3) a disposition the subsection does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 759(4) the decision has the same force and effect as a decision of the trial court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 759(4) the decision has the same force and effect as a decision of the trial court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 759(6) the day the sentence is deemed to have commenced` TRUE (Date 3 3 2019) EQUALS JUST (Date 3 3 2019)   -- the day the trial court sentenced the offender
#ASSERT `s 759(6) the day the sentence is deemed to have commenced` FALSE (Date 3 3 2019) EQUALS NOTHING   -- a sentence not imposed by the court of appeal under this section
#ASSERT `s 759(7) the provisions of Part XXI with respect to procedure on appeals apply to the appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 759(7) the provisions of Part XXI with respect to procedure on appeals apply to the appeal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 760: disclosure to the Correctional Service of Canada`

#ASSERT `s 760 the court shall order that the reports, testimony, observations and transcript be forwarded to the Correctional Service of Canada` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 760 the court shall order that the reports, testimony, observations and transcript be forwarded to the Correctional Service of Canada` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no finding of a dangerous offender or a long-term offender
#TRACE `s 760 the court's duty to order disclosure to the Correctional Service of Canada` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 760 order that a copy of the reports, testimony, observations and transcript be forwarded to the Correctional Service of Canada for information` AT 5

#TRACE `s 760 the court's duty to order disclosure to the Correctional Service of Canada` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

§ `s 761: review for parole`

#ASSERT `s 761(1) the day on which seven years from the day the person was taken into custody have expired` (Date 1 3 2015) EQUALS Date 1 3 2022
#ASSERT `s 761(1) the day on which seven years from the day the person was taken into custody have expired` (Date 29 2 2016) EQUALS Date 28 2 2023   -- seven years after a leap day: the day is clamped to the last day of February
#ASSERT `s 761(1) the last day for the next review` (Date 1 3 2022) EQUALS Date 1 3 2024
#ASSERT `s 761(1) the last day for the next review` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026   -- two years after a leap day
#ASSERT `s 761(1) the Parole Board of Canada shall review the condition, history and circumstances of the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 761(1) the Parole Board of Canada shall review the condition, history and circumstances of the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- subject to subsection (2): imposed before October 15, 1977
#ASSERT `s 761(1) the Parole Board of Canada shall review the condition, history and circumstances of the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not in custody under an indeterminate sentence
#ASSERT `s 761(1) the first review is after the expiration of seven years` (Date 1 3 2015) (Date 1 3 2022) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- on the day seven years have expired
#ASSERT `s 761(1) the first review is after the expiration of seven years` (Date 1 3 2015) (Date 28 2 2022) EQUALS NOTHING   -- a day before: the subsection is silent about an earlier review
#ASSERT `s 761(1) the review is not later than two years after the previous review` (Date 1 3 2022) (Date 1 3 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last day
#ASSERT `s 761(1) the review is not later than two years after the previous review` (Date 1 3 2022) (Date 2 3 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a day after
#ASSERT `s 761(1) the review is not later than two years after the previous review` (Date 1 3 2022) (Date 1 3 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#TRACE `s 761(1) the duty of the Parole Board of Canada to review the person again` (Date 1 3 2022) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Parole Board of Canada` DOES `s 761 review the condition, history and circumstances of the person for the purpose of determining whether the person should be granted parole` AT 731

#TRACE `s 761(1) the duty of the Parole Board of Canada to review the person again` (Date 1 3 2022) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Parole Board of Canada` DOES `s 761 review the condition, history and circumstances of the person for the purpose of determining whether the person should be granted parole` AT 732

#ASSERT `s 761(2) the Parole Board of Canada shall review the condition, history and circumstances of the person at least once in every year` TRUE (Date 14 10 1977) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last day before October 15, 1977
#ASSERT `s 761(2) the Parole Board of Canada shall review the condition, history and circumstances of the person at least once in every year` TRUE (Date 15 10 1977) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- on October 15, 1977 the text no longer reaches ("before October 15, 1977")
#ASSERT `s 761(2) the Parole Board of Canada shall review the condition, history and circumstances of the person at least once in every year` FALSE (Date 14 10 1977) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not in custody under an indeterminate sentence
#ASSERT `s 761(2) the last day for the next review` (Date 1 3 2022) EQUALS Date 1 3 2023
#ASSERT `s 761(2) the review is within a year of the previous review` (Date 1 3 2022) (Date 1 3 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 761(2) the review is within a year of the previous review` (Date 1 3 2022) (Date 2 3 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 761(2) the duty of the Parole Board of Canada to review the person at least once in every year` (Date 1 3 2022) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Parole Board of Canada` DOES `s 761 review the condition, history and circumstances of the person for the purpose of determining whether the person should be granted parole` AT 365

#TRACE `s 761(2) the duty of the Parole Board of Canada to review the person at least once in every year` (Date 1 3 2022) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 366)
